WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.630
Inherited will...

3
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.540
the tides of time,
and humanity's dreams...

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.370
They cannot be stopped.

5
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.480
As long as people seek freedom,

6
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.110
these things will never cease to be.

7
00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.820
Tony is a decoy?

8
00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.920
Yeah. He'll be fine.

9
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.550
Let's hurry, Vivi.

10
00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.970
Explain the situation to me.

11
00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.310
But Sanji,
didn't you get shot back there?

12
00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.540
Hm?

13
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.830
Me?

14
00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.570
Hello?

15
00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.070
We've caught him!

16
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.840
What should we do
with this strange man?!

17
00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.200
Where are you? Tell me!

18
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:24.660
Th-The front gate of a casino 
in Rainbase named Rain Dinners!

19
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.750
All right, nicely done. 
That was a star performance.

20
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.830
Now your boss will show up here.

21
00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.840
Th-Thanks so much...
So, can I go now?

22
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.470
No, sir.

23
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.220
Yeah, guess not...

24
00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.720
Look, Chopper.

25
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.520
His buddies are regrouping
where we were just running wild.

26
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.310
Who are you?

27
00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.940
M-My name is Mr. Prince.

28
00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:01.450
Huh? So then, you're the one 
who did all this to my companions?

29
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.600
Whatever I can manage...

30
00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.790
My name is Mr. Prince!

31
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.920
My name is Mr. Prince!

32
00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.510
What is the meaning of this?

33
00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.440
I-It was a man, 
calling himself Mr. Prince...

34
00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:40.990
Him?!

35
00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.500
Bad news! The bridge collapsed!

36
00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.680
And that's more 
or less what happened.

37
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.060
Is Tony all right?

38
00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.060
Yeah.

39
00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.060
He has some tricks
up his sleeve, after all.

40
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:24.160
You bastard...
Where did you go, Mr. Prince?

41
00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.040
I swear I'm going to 
find you and kill you.

42
00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.620
Careful, now... Heart pounding...

43
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.170
Ahhh!

44
00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.550
– We're gonna die! We're gonna die!
– The water! The water!

45
00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.010
Once this cage is submerged, 
it's all over for us!

46
00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:48.680
Hey, you stupid gator! 
Come and get me!

47
00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.810
Are you insane, Nami?!

48
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.520
I'm goading him so he'll
bite this cage to pieces!

49
00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.110
I get it! Great idea!

50
00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:02.530
Come and get me, you stupid banana!
You rotten banana!

51
00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.820
No, that's wrong! I told you, 
he's basically an alligator,

52
00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.320
but with a banana on his head.

53
00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.280
What?! Would you shut up?

54
00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.000
For example,
there's the monkey dance, right?

55
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.830
You rotten banana!

56
00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.460
Listen to what I'm saying!

57
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.460
What?

58
00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.340
For example,
there's the monkey dance, right?

59
00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.760
A monkey is an animal, but the
monkey dance is a dance, and–

60
00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.010
Don't touch that! 
Learn something, will you?!

61
00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.260
But can't you eat both
alligators and bananas?!

62
00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.180
Here he comes!

63
00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.150
It's no use!

64
00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.110
What a tough cage!

65
00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.240
Vivi! Please hurry!

66
00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.990
Hey, you guys...

67
00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:46.530
Huh?

68
00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:49.700
How can you stay so composed?!

69
00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.290
You think up something too!

70
00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:58.210
How much do you guys know? 
What exactly is Crocodile after?

71
00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.840
That woman who was 
at Crocodile's side...

72
00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.010
The World Government put a price
on her head going back 20 years.

73
00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.380
The amount was over 
70 million, as I recall.

74
00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.930
S-Seventy million?!

75
00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.140
S-So what about it?

76
00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.560
That's as high as Crocodile's...

77
00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.140
The moment those two joined forces,

78
00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.350
this became more than 
just a simple coup.

79
00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:21.810
If left alone,

80
00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.990
they'll escalate this into something
that'll involve the entire world.

81
00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:29.110
The entire world? 
What do you mean?

82
00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.570
That does seem a little far-fetched.

83
00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.080
What're you guys talking about?

84
00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.080
Huh?

85
00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:37.870
I'm just here to kick his ass!
All those other reasons don't matter!

86
00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.840
I see...

87
00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.130
So, how are we getting out of here?

88
00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.680
It's up to my thighs!

89
00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.260
We're gonna die! We're gonna die!

90
00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.470
I can't handle this much longer...

91
00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:01.690
This is bad! This is bad! 
Tough it out! Didn't Vivi say so?!

92
00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.690
Must be hard for you, huh, Vivi?

93
00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.980
I'm sorry, I know you 
don't have time for this.

94
00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.030
Damn it!

95
00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.950
If I were just a better swordsman,
this cage would be nothing!

96
00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:17.910
You should try your hardest
to dine a little more quietly.

97
00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.120
Huh?

98
00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.880
Anti-Manner Kick Course!

99
00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.620
Hey there.

100
00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.210
Been waiting long?

101
00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.330
– Ahhh! Prince!
– Ahhh! Prince!

102
00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.630
Thank goodness.

103
00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:10.300
Stop goofing around 
and find the key already!

104
00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.300
Nami!

105
00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.630
D-Do you love me now?!

106
00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.470
Yeah, yeah, I'm in love, 
now hurry and open this up!

107
00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.970
Okay!

108
00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.270
His idiocy knows no bounds, huh?

109
00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.270
Mellorine! Mellorine!

110
00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:25.020
Vivi! Way to go!

111
00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.440
Yeah!

112
00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.450
Here they come, one after the next.

113
00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:37.280
Go, Sanji! Pound them all!

114
00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.950
Feel free to bunch up together

115
00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.460
and come at me,
you damn bananas.

116
00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.920
Anyone with manners as poor
as yours, who would attack a lady,

117
00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:51.920
gets some table manners
beaten into them well and good.

118
00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.880
Sanji! There isn't any time for that!

119
00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.180
One-second strikes! 
No, make that one-instant strikes!

120
00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.810
Take out the third one
who just came in.

121
00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.480
What? You can tell?

122
00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.730
Are your ears just for show?

123
00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.980
Its growl belongs to the one
that swallowed the key.

124
00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:12.280
Collapsing the bridge bought
 them some time. Clever.

125
00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.280
They have more crewmates here.

126
00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:19.780
So they lured us away to get
to the room with their comrades?

127
00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.240
Probably.

128
00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.290
There it is!

129
00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.210
The key to the cage!

130
00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:33.710
What is that?!

131
00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.010
That doesn't look like a key!

132
00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.970
Wax-Wax Ball!

133
00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.220
Release!

134
00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:41.930
Ah!

135
00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.220
What?!

136
00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:48.190
Oh! W-Water! It's water! 
It's a miracle!

137
00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.860
Hey, it's him!

138
00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.690
3! It's 3!

139
00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:57.110
Mr. 3! What was he doing 
in the belly of an alligator?!

140
00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.290
I'm alive again! 
I thought I was dead back there!

141
00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:09.420
That vile Crocodile! 
He may have tried to get rid of me,

142
00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.670
but he didn't try hard enough! 
The moment I was swallowed,

143
00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:17.050
I squeezed out the last of my power 
to create this Wax-Wax ball.

144
00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.050
What's this?

145
00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:25.890
Hand that key over to us!

146
00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.600
Ahhh! It's you guys!

147
00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.730
What? This key...?

148
00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.610
Hold on...

149
00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.200
A room, forcefully leaking water...

150
00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:44.160
an iron cage... and this key...

151
00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.620
I know what's going on, now.

152
00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.580
You're Mr. 3, are you?

153
00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.920
You startled me!

154
00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:59.760
Are you Mr. 3? 
Hand over the key, quietly.

155
00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:03.140
Gleam!

156
00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:07.430
Here comes a long throw!

157
00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.930
What?!

158
00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:19.490
I don't know who you are, 
but you appear to be on their side!

159
00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.570
If you want the key, go find it!

160
00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:26.040
However, don't hold me
responsible if you can't find it!

161
00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.290
You bastard...

162
00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.920
What if this person is able to

163
00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.790
pick out the alligator 
that swallowed the key?

164
00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.540
Hmph, it wouldn't do any good.

165
00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.210
Even if they were lucky 
enough to get that key,

166
00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:44.090
the real key is right here. Let them
struggle as hard as they want.

167
00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.180
You are bad.

168
00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.930
Just a minute, Sanji!

169
00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:52.940
Couldn't his Wax-Wax power
make a key to this cage?

170
00:11:58.820 --> 00:11:59.860
Indeed.

171
00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.910
Nicely done, candle man.

172
00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.220
Let's get moving.
There's little time.

173
00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:26.050
Yeah. I'm sure the first route 
they took is toward Alubarna.

174
00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.560
But it's nothing but
bananagators that way!

175
00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:36.440
Aren't there any more?! 
That wasn't enough!

176
00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.440
Nothing to worry about...

177
00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.700
I was unable to take out
even one of them!

178
00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:46.700
No, no! Those guys are abnormally
strong, so don't take it personally!

179
00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:50.830
Dammit, I can't go all out, 
soaked in water like this!

180
00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.590
The walls are crumbling!

181
00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.600
Idiot, that's overdoing it.

182
00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.680
The passageway is crumbling, too!

183
00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.060
Out! We're getting out of here!

184
00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.780
These small-timers are going to pay!

185
00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.290
I'll kill them all with my own hands,
right here, right now!

186
00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.380
What...?

187
00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:42.360
<b>Catch you later,
you damn gator.</b>
<b>~Mr. Prince</b>

188
00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.810
Hey, you still alive, Luffy?

189
00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.690
Usopp, wake up!

190
00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:09.370
Good grief, what are you doing?! 
Swim, like you're supposed to!

191
00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:14.370
Man, those abilities of yours
sure have their downsides, huh?

192
00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.960
Whoa, Smoker!

193
00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.500
Hey now, Zoro, what are you
bringing the enemy along for?!

194
00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:28.470
Back off! I didn't want to. 
He was this close to dying, after all.

195
00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:32.930
Whatever. Let's just hurry on ahead.

196
00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.430
We've lost quite a bit of time.
Vivi, can we still make it?

197
00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:37.480
I don't know.

198
00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.560
Nami...

199
00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.770
Do you still have
that perfume from Nanohana?

200
00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:44.400
Huh? Yeah. Why?

201
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.360
Put some of it on.

202
00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:48.650
Like this?

203
00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.740
Ah! I love you to the
ends of the world!

204
00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.700
Come on, get going, seriously.

205
00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.700
Roronoa!

206
00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.480
Why did you save my life?

207
00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.110
Hey, Zoro! Save him!

208
00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.740
Huh?! He's our enemy!
Just leave him!

209
00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.240
If we just leave him,
he'll die, you know!

210
00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.320
He can't swim!

211
00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.450
Yeah, well, I know that...

212
00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.250
but he's...!

213
00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.920
I was just following 
the captain's orders.

214
00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.750
I don't think you necessarily
have to thank me.

215
00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.720
It was one of his whims. 
Don't overthink it.

216
00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:57.810
Then, you'd have no gripes with me 
carrying out my duties here, right?

217
00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:02.230
See? Didn't I tell you? That's what
you get for saving a marine.

218
00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.400
They're here?
The Straw Hat Pirates?

219
00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.160
Yeah! Captain Smoker 
is with them now!

220
00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.240
Let's go back him up!

221
00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:23.170
All right, men!
Full speed to Alubarna!

222
00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.210
Where is Crocodile?!

223
00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.710
Ah, they came around.

224
00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.510
Smokey! You want some of this?!

225
00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.520
Ahh! It's Smoker!

226
00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.480
Hey, Luffy, don't do it! 
Let's scram!

227
00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:45.440
Is this guy for real?

228
00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.280
This way! Hurry!

229
00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.250
Go.

230
00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:09.670
But this is the only time
I'm letting you off.

231
00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:12.880
Next time we meet, 
consider yourselves dead.

232
00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.690
There they are!

233
00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:36.150
Don't let them escape!

234
00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:39.740
Come on, let's go. 
The marines are coming.

235
00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.120
Which way is Alubarna?

236
00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.620
That way! We head due east!

237
00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.540
Hey, Luffy! Hurry! 
What are you doing?!

238
00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.000
Yeah...

239
00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.640
They won't get away this time!

240
00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:06.560
You know,
you're not so unlikable!

241
00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:17.400
Get the hell outta here!

242
00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:33.920
Don't let them get away!

243
00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:00.240
I see them!

244
00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.030
After them!

245
00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.540
After them!

246
00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.380
Captain, aren't you going after them?

247
00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.340
No. I'm too tired.

248
00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:23.550
You're too tired?

249
00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:24.390
Hey...

250
00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:25.100
Sir!

251
00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.850
It's no use going after those guys. 
Tell our men to stop.

252
00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.020
Have them regroup here.
Contact headquarters too.

253
00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:39.030
We'll request that they dispatch
all military vessels in the vicinity

254
00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.450
to this country,
the Kingdom of Arabasta.

255
00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.160
You're calling for reinforcements...?

256
00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:45.280
But Captain,

257
00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:48.320
I'm not sure our superiors
will be willing to move ships

258
00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.500
against such a small pirate group.

259
00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.460
Do I look like a man who cares
what the top brass thinks?!

260
00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.540
Uh, y-yes, sir! Right away!

261
00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:01.010
Hey! Come back! Come back here!

262
00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.270
Hurry!

263
00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:22.240
Mm-hmm, this way. The scent 
of Nami's perfume is getting stronger.

264
00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:24.910
Hey, we're not actually

265
00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.910
gonna run the entire way
to Alubarna, are we?!

266
00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.830
That's right! Eyelashes!

267
00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.080
Where has Eyelashes gone?!

268
00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.000
Now that you mention it,

269
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.500
this town should have 
a stable or something!

270
00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.840
Let's get horses!

271
00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.460
But the marines are in town.

272
00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.260
Not to worry.
Look in front of you.

273
00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.470
Hey, guys!

274
00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.020
A crab?!

275
00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.100
Chopper!

276
00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.350
That's a moving crab!

277
00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.400
Looks yummy!

278
00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.750
Awesome! Awesome! 
Awesome! That's awesome!

279
00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:14.000
Hop on board!

280
00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.420
We get to ride it?! Woo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

281
00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:18.920
Nice to meetcha!

282
00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.250
Its face looks kind of iffy,
doesn't it?

283
00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.920
And you've got yet another 
amazing thing in tow, huh?

284
00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.820
He's Eyelashes' friend.

285
00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:35.140
Eyelashes was born in this town
and has lots of friends in the area.

286
00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.310
He is kind of pervy, though.

287
00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:42.320
Amazing! Moving crabs are 
usually submerged under the sand,

288
00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:44.240
so these crabs are like phantoms!

289
00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:47.110
But he's pretty fast...
isn't he?

290
00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:49.910
Guys, hang on tight!

291
00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.660
Alright, let's go! We're off!

292
00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:05.340
What?!

293
00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:08.090
Stop, Chopper!

294
00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:16.690
It's him! Why, you...!

295
00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:23.980
Hey! Luffy!

296
00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:24.940
That idiot!

297
00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:26.570
Luffy!

298
00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:32.580
You guys go on ahead! 
I'll take care of things here!

299
00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:48.130
Make sure you deliver Vivi
back to her home! Make sure!

300
00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:53.060
Just make sure.

301
00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:56.270
That idiot...

302
00:22:56.980 --> 00:22:57.810
Hey!

303
00:22:57.810 --> 00:23:00.730
Go, Chopper!
Keep steady toward Alubarna!

304
00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:03.570
G-Got it.

305
00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:04.730
We're off!

306
00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:07.780
Hold on...!

307
00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:08.450
Hey!

308
00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:10.740
Hey, Zoro!
Are we leaving him behind?!

309
00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:12.490
Hey, that's cold!

310
00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.240
Luffy!

311
00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:17.450
It's all right, Vivi!
He'll be fine!

312
00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:19.830
I feel sorry for the other two.

313
00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:22.830
After all, there isn't a single person

314
00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:26.170
who's come out unscathed once Luffy
has set his sights on them.

315
00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:31.640
Listen to me, Vivi. He'll for sure
tame him... that Crocodile.

316
00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:34.390
The moment that 
the Rebel Army started running,

317
00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:36.600
the time limit on this land was set.

318
00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:40.810
Once the Royal Army 
and the Rebel Army meet,

319
00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:44.560
this land, the Kingdom 
of Arabasta, will be gone.

320
00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:48.070
If you are the one and only
hope for preventing that,

321
00:23:49.070 --> 00:23:51.530
then you have to survive, at all costs.

322
00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:57.990
It doesn't matter what might happen
to any of us from this point on!

323
00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:01.870
B-But...

324
00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:09.880
Vivi, this is a fight that you started.

325
00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:13.840
Several years ago,
you departed Arabasta and

326
00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:16.470
challenged this unknown 
organization to battle.

327
00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:18.810
However...

328
00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:22.680
don't go thinking that 
you're fighting alone anymore.

329
00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:31.990
Ah! V-V-Vivi! Don't you wor... wor... 
 Don't worry! I'm g-gonna...

330
00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:37.330
Luffy!

331
00:24:34.700 --> 00:24:37.340
...Luffy!

332
00:24:37.340 --> 00:24:37.910
Huh?

333
00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:40.910
We'll be waiting for you
in Alubarna, okay?!

334
00:24:40.910 --> 00:24:44.480
...okay?! ...okay?!

335
00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:45.380
Yeah!

336
00:24:56.260 --> 00:24:59.060
Princess Vivi got the slip on us, huh?

337
00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:03.730
Either way, our agents are
scheduled to gather in Alubarna.

338
00:25:04.480 --> 00:25:06.270
Contact them at once.

339
00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:13.950
And now... You've taken this
nonsense too far, Straw Hat Luffy.

340
00:25:17.570 --> 00:25:19.740
Well, what she does is try...

341
00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:24.370
to help everyone along her way,
no matter how weak she is.

342
00:25:26.370 --> 00:25:29.790
The thought of abandoning someone
just wrenches her heart.

343
00:25:30.300 --> 00:25:33.800
She thinks that no one needs 
to die in this rebellion.

344
00:25:33.800 --> 00:25:36.380
Nobody needs to die?

345
00:25:36.380 --> 00:25:39.720
There are many maudlin, 
peace-loving fools like that.

346
00:25:40.760 --> 00:25:43.770
Those are people who have
never seen true battle.

347
00:25:43.770 --> 00:25:45.770
Wouldn't you agree?

348
00:25:45.770 --> 00:25:47.230
Yup.

349
00:25:50.690 --> 00:25:55.740
But as long as you're here,
she'll come after you until she's dead.

350
00:25:58.320 --> 00:25:59.450
That's why...

351
00:25:59.450 --> 00:26:01.580
I'm gonna stop you right here!

352
00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:06.540
That's worse than nonsense.

353
00:26:07.210 --> 00:26:11.500
You're the biggest fool of them all,
kid. What an example you are.

354
00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:14.960
You get close to someone, 
and then die because of it.

355
00:26:15.510 --> 00:26:20.930
I've forsaken tons of people like that.

356
00:26:21.470 --> 00:26:22.930
In that case...

357
00:26:22.930 --> 00:26:25.140
doesn't that make you the fool?

358
00:26:29.600 --> 00:26:31.560
Find something funny?

359
00:26:32.070 --> 00:26:35.400
You want to die too,
Nico Robin?

360
00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:38.110
If you feel like it, go right ahead.

361
00:26:38.110 --> 00:26:41.410
Besides, didn't you promise 
not to call me by that name?

362
00:26:41.410 --> 00:26:42.580
Where are you going?

363
00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:45.450
I'm going on ahead to Alubarna.

364
00:26:46.250 --> 00:26:48.540
I can't figure that woman out.

365
00:26:51.790 --> 00:26:53.590
I'll give you three minutes.

366
00:26:57.340 --> 00:26:59.010
I don't have time...

367
00:26:59.510 --> 00:27:02.640
to mess with you 
any longer than that.

368
00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:12.060
You don't mind, do you?

369
00:27:13.360 --> 00:27:15.280
No, that's fine.

370
00:27:16.530 --> 00:27:18.570
Gum-Gum...

371
00:27:18.570 --> 00:27:19.740
Pistol!

372
00:27:31.460 --> 00:27:32.580
Oh?

373
00:27:32.580 --> 00:27:34.130
Gum-Gum...

374
00:27:35.040 --> 00:27:36.630
Stamp!

375
00:27:46.890 --> 00:27:52.060
I should warn you, Straw Hat Luffy, 
that no matter how hard you try,

376
00:27:52.060 --> 00:27:54.860
there is no way 
you'll ever beat me.

377
00:27:54.860 --> 00:27:58.030
Gum-Gum Gatling!

378
00:28:15.340 --> 00:28:17.750
Listen here, Straw Hat Luffy.

379
00:28:17.750 --> 00:28:20.340
You can continue hitting me

380
00:28:20.340 --> 00:28:22.300
with these mosquito-bite attacks,

381
00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:23.590
but you will never–

382
00:28:23.590 --> 00:28:25.140
Gum-Gum...

383
00:28:25.930 --> 00:28:28.470
Bazooka!

384
00:28:33.100 --> 00:28:34.940
Battle Axe!

385
00:28:46.870 --> 00:28:49.830
Why, you... you... you...! 
Did that smash you?!

386
00:28:49.830 --> 00:28:51.700
You sand croc!

387
00:28:54.870 --> 00:28:57.670
I told you, that won't work.

388
00:28:58.290 --> 00:28:59.550
You bastard...!

389
00:28:59.550 --> 00:29:03.680
No matter how hard 
a rubber man like you might try,

390
00:29:03.680 --> 00:29:05.800
there is no way...

391
00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.390
you'll ever defe–

392
00:29:09.350 --> 00:29:12.730
"Defe"? What's that?
Can't understand you!

393
00:29:22.320 --> 00:29:25.660
I think that is just about
enough fun and games,

394
00:29:26.490 --> 00:29:28.120
Straw Hat Luffy.

395
00:29:28.120 --> 00:29:30.940
I've been taking this seriously 
the whole time!

396
00:29:31.830 --> 00:29:35.960
But this is a problem.
There's just no hitting him.

397
00:29:35.960 --> 00:29:37.750
He's all dry and sandy.

398
00:29:37.750 --> 00:29:41.960
As a pirate,
I outclass you in every way!

399
00:29:42.510 --> 00:29:44.510
Desert Spada!

400
00:29:53.850 --> 00:29:55.690
O-Ow!

401
00:29:55.690 --> 00:29:58.020
Good call on your part.

402
00:29:58.020 --> 00:30:01.150
Taking it head-on would have
elicited more than just an "ow."

403
00:30:03.150 --> 00:30:06.110
What the...?!
That thing split the desert in two!

404
00:30:06.110 --> 00:30:09.530
Devil fruit abilities must be trained and honed

405
00:30:09.530 --> 00:30:13.080
until they are powerful enough
to rival any weapon.

406
00:30:13.540 --> 00:30:17.320
Do not take me for the fools who are
satisfied with their powers as is...

407
00:30:18.540 --> 00:30:22.710
And now, it's time you
regret ever defying me.

408
00:30:26.380 --> 00:30:28.840
Desert Girasole!

409
00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:43.520
What?! What?! What?! What?!

410
00:30:49.450 --> 00:30:53.450
The sand! It's sucking me
into the ground!

411
00:30:59.370 --> 00:31:02.040
Never heard of quicksand?

412
00:31:02.790 --> 00:31:06.840
It makes for a handy desert coffin, 
with no need for a tombstone.

413
00:31:06.840 --> 00:31:10.430
The sand is drawn down 
into underground waterways.

414
00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:14.810
I am able to detect where those are.

415
00:31:14.810 --> 00:31:19.190
No one in the world can stand up 
to me when fighting in the desert.

416
00:31:22.150 --> 00:31:23.360
I'm not about...

417
00:31:25.110 --> 00:31:27.820
to let myself be buried alive in sand!

418
00:31:29.780 --> 00:31:31.740
You bastard!

419
00:31:31.740 --> 00:31:33.780
Gum-Gum...

420
00:31:33.780 --> 00:31:35.620
Bazooka!

421
00:31:37.080 --> 00:31:40.620
If I can't hit you, 
then how about I catch you?

422
00:31:40.620 --> 00:31:41.540
Gum-Gum...

423
00:31:41.540 --> 00:31:44.000
Finger Net!

424
00:31:46.000 --> 00:31:50.720
Are you just incapable of learning?
That won't work.

425
00:31:50.720 --> 00:31:52.010
Gum-Gum...

426
00:31:52.010 --> 00:31:54.050
Whip!

427
00:31:56.310 --> 00:31:58.640
Are you planning to keep doing that?

428
00:32:00.560 --> 00:32:02.020
Let go of me, you bastard!

429
00:32:02.980 --> 00:32:04.360
Barján!

430
00:32:09.320 --> 00:32:10.990
M-My arm!

431
00:32:16.740 --> 00:32:18.660
My arm...! My arm...!

432
00:32:18.660 --> 00:32:21.870
It's turned into a mummy! 
My arm has become a mummy!

433
00:32:21.870 --> 00:32:23.880
Because of the sand.

434
00:32:23.880 --> 00:32:27.380
The hydration in your arm 
has been sucked out.

435
00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:32.840
I could wring every drop of water out
of you until you're shriveled and dead.

436
00:32:33.890 --> 00:32:36.800
That is how the desert works too.

437
00:32:38.060 --> 00:32:39.560
Y-You've gotta be kidding me!

438
00:32:41.020 --> 00:32:43.310
I know! Water!

439
00:32:49.860 --> 00:32:51.490
That was worthless.

440
00:32:51.490 --> 00:32:52.950
Nothing worthless about it!

441
00:32:52.950 --> 00:32:56.160
The dried-up old man 
in Yuba spent all night

442
00:32:56.160 --> 00:32:58.990
preparing this water for me!

443
00:32:58.990 --> 00:33:00.290
Luffy-kun.

444
00:33:00.290 --> 00:33:01.910
Take this with you.

445
00:33:01.910 --> 00:33:04.620
The old guy told me...

446
00:33:06.830 --> 00:33:09.880
Yuba wasn't going to 
give in to the sand.

447
00:33:09.880 --> 00:33:11.480
Gum-Gum...

448
00:33:12.300 --> 00:33:14.340
Are you still planning 
to do something?

449
00:33:14.340 --> 00:33:16.340
Munch Munch!

450
00:33:22.100 --> 00:33:24.850
What kind of nonsense
are you trying to pull?!

451
00:33:29.020 --> 00:33:34.320
Die. You, along with 
the indomitable land of Yuba.

452
00:33:35.990 --> 00:33:40.370
Your three minutes are up. 
I told you when we got started,

453
00:33:40.370 --> 00:33:43.540
I just don't have the time
to entertain you any longer.

454
00:33:44.290 --> 00:33:46.210
Sables!

455
00:34:02.770 --> 00:34:05.640
The sand is nice and dry.

456
00:34:05.730 --> 00:34:08.650
<b>Rainbase</b>

457
00:34:06.230 --> 00:34:08.650
Sandstorm!
I see a sandstorm to the south!

458
00:34:08.650 --> 00:34:09.860
Take shelter!

459
00:34:09.860 --> 00:34:13.610
Wait, the sandstorm isn't
coming this way! It's heading south!

460
00:34:13.610 --> 00:34:16.530
Captain Smoker, over there!

461
00:34:21.740 --> 00:34:24.000
Vivi, what's wrong?

462
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:26.870
There's a sandstorm 
over toward Rainbase!

463
00:34:28.250 --> 00:34:29.670
It's him.

464
00:34:33.090 --> 00:34:34.590
Luffy...

465
00:34:42.350 --> 00:34:44.680
Listen here, Straw Hat Luffy.

466
00:34:44.680 --> 00:34:49.440
The prevailing winds here always blow 
from north to south.

467
00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:53.320
Now if this baby sandstorm were to catch hold of the winds,

468
00:34:53.320 --> 00:34:56.900
gaining in size and strength
as it headed south,

469
00:34:56.900 --> 00:35:00.530
just where do you think
this enlarged sandstorm will hit?

470
00:35:01.910 --> 00:35:03.780
South, you say?

471
00:35:04.700 --> 00:35:05.750
Yuba.

472
00:35:09.120 --> 00:35:10.500
Why?!

473
00:35:11.710 --> 00:35:14.500
Hey, you!
What are you doing?! Stop it!

474
00:35:15.670 --> 00:35:18.970
Look. Little by little, 
it's starting to head south.

475
00:35:18.970 --> 00:35:21.930
That dried-up old man 
has nothing to do with this!

476
00:35:23.050 --> 00:35:26.470
Why, you...! Stop it, you!

477
00:35:27.060 --> 00:35:29.440
Stop, you bastard! Stop!

478
00:35:33.060 --> 00:35:35.360
Give it up, it won't work.

479
00:35:35.900 --> 00:35:38.320
That sandstorm will pick up strength,

480
00:35:38.320 --> 00:35:42.320
and obtain wind speeds 
that even I can't stop.

481
00:35:42.320 --> 00:35:44.660
You've gotta be kidding me!

482
00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:47.500
Yuba is finished.

483
00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:49.660
Stop it! Right now! Stop–

484
00:35:59.760 --> 00:36:02.800
Who do you think
you're ordering around?

485
00:36:07.100 --> 00:36:11.390
There are any number 
of rookies like you...

486
00:36:11.390 --> 00:36:14.360
who are nothing but talk...

487
00:36:14.360 --> 00:36:16.690
Straw Hat Luffy...

488
00:36:17.650 --> 00:36:21.280
here in the Grand Line.

